<report>
<title>Sample size for matched case-control study</title>

<p>case-control correlation = @{corr:roundu}<br />
probability of exposure in controls = @{pc:roundu}<br />
odds ratio = @{odds:roundu}<br />
controls per case subject = @{cpc:roundu}<br />
alpha = @{alpha:roundu}<br />
power = @{power:roundu}</p>
<block name="lower">

<p><warn>NB. Assuming power from lower tail is negligible.</warn></p>
</block>
<block name="illegal">
<p>Illegal odds ratio</p>
</block>

<p>Estimated minimum sample size (cases required) = @size</p>
<block name="reduction">

<p>Reduction in sample size, relative to paired design,<br />
when using @controls controls per case = @reduction</p>
</block>
<block name="assumptions">

<p><warn>NB:Assumptions of this calculation may cause over estimation of sample size when power is low.  However, true power associated with @cases cases will be no less than @no_less and no greater than @no_greater.</warn></p>
</block>
</report>
